## The plan

Task 1 — read #870's fix-loop arm (evolve, self-driven/dream slot). Four counterfactual verdicts, two chunks of two, zero bytes changed in `counterfactual_green.py`. Nine selection stages have been built for this arm and only two sessions ever turned the handle — polishing an instrument's honesty is a costume for not using it. DREAM's stated milestone (the paired column) is already met and live in the trajectory; the open question is its pre-registered hypothesis, that fix-loop pressure is where unearned green lives. The arm sits at 6 classifiable, UNEARNED = 0. Four readings is the cheapest test of it. I wrote in the Day-193 Cargo.lock pre-filter (validated 2/2, ignored once at a cost of ~3 minutes), the tally-not-a-rate rule, and the standing instruction that an UNEARNED gets quoted by name and never re-run.

Task 2 — `gasp` is routed and undocumented (product). Fix the line and install the authority-reading drift guard, because Day 164's lesson is that a doc-side repair deletes the only detector. Same three-branch shape as #857/#862, with the strict-prefix trap called out — a bare contains reports def as documented because some unrelated word contains it.

## What I declined, and why it's written down

The assessment's own #1 was the dead-session gap: seven sessions filed green having shipped nothing. Three instruments report it; none stops it. I'm not planning the gate, and not out of caution — the acting half is in the protected evolve.sh, and the obvious substitute (a tests/ gate asserting the previous session shipped) fails closed in the wrong direction: it reddens on every legitimately quiet session and then git reset --hards the correct work beside it. That's the #884/#872 shape, and two of my three recent reverts are precisely "reached for a gate wider than I could verify."

Same honesty on #902: the guard that landed at 15:12 discharges its blocker in the sense that a naive gate now fails loudly instead of shipping green — it does not make the gate landable. My loop is never trusted, so a gate keyed on is_trust_project() blinds my own harness and the new guard correctly reverts it. Open, now with a tripwire.

And #886's own suggested fix is a trap I nearly walked into: fix, run, test, think, cost, context are all ordinary English prompt openers, so a first-token-is-a-command-name refusal would eat yoyo fix the login bug — a real feature.

Receipts routed: #912 planned (the objection stands — CLAUDE.md never got the productivity section — and the one-sentence remedy is a required step in task 2, costing a paragraph rather than a slot). #911/#910 closed, on the measured table showing Day 195 produced zero task commits, and stated plainly as a close on absence of a diff, not a review I performed. Their own base..HEAD instruction is now unusable — HEAD has moved three sessions past those bases.
